    {
      "id": "get-persistent-index",
      "name": "GetPersistentIndex",
      "category": "PrimitiveSceneInfo",
      "signature": "GetPersistentIndex(Target)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FPrimitiveSceneInfo*"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "FPersistentPrimitiveIndex",
      "docs": "Persistent index of the primitive in the range [0, FScene::GetMaxPersistentPrimitiveIndex() ). Where the max is never higher than the high watermark of the primitives in the scene.\nThis index remains stable for the life-time of the primitive in the scene (i.e., same as PrimitiveSceneInfo and Proxy - between FScene::AddPrimitive / FScene::RemovePrimitive).\nThe intended use is to enable tracking primitive data over time in renderer systems using direct indexing, e.g., for efficiently storing a bit per primitive.\nDirect indexing also facilitates easy GPU-reflection and access of the persistent data, where it can be accessed as e.g., GetPrimitiveData(...).PersistentPrimitiveIndex.\nIt is allocated using FScene::PersistentPrimitiveIdAllocator from a range with holes that is kept as compact as possible up to the high-water mark of the scene primitives.\nDue to persistence this maximum can be substantially larger than the current number of Primitives at times, but never worse than the high-watermark.\nIn the future, the index will likely be refactored to persist for the lifetime of the component (to facilitate tracking data past proxy re-creates).\nNote: It is not currently used to index any of the current FScene primitive arrays (use PackedIndex), though this is intended to change."
    },
